course: dictionary
lesson: 14970
title: Feeling sorry: remorse
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Remorse is a deep, painful feeling of being sorry for something wrong you have done. It is more than a quick "oops". You feel it inside, and it makes you want to put things right.
explain: «Mia felt remorse after she broke her brother's model ship.» She did something wrong, and now she feels bad about it deep down. Remorse is a noun, so you can feel it, show it or be full of it.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like sorry, guilty or "I wish I had not" often point to remorse. «He hung his head, full of remorse, and said, "I should not have lied."» The hung head and the apology show the feeling.
explain: Remorse is often the first step to making things right. You say sorry, you try to repair the harm, and you try not to do it again. Remorse on its own can fade, as Toad's does in the stories.
fact: Remorse is a noun: you can feel remorse, show remorse or be full of remorse.
fact: «Remorse» means a deep, painful feeling of being sorry and guilty for something wrong you have done.
fact: «Without remorse» is an idiom meaning cruelly, without feeling sorry.
fact: Remorse is often the first step to saying sorry, making things right and being forgiven.
fact: Judges sometimes think about whether a person shows remorse when they decide a case.
exercise: «Sam broke the vase and felt remorse all evening.» What does remorse mean here? | *Deep, painful sorry for doing something wrong | A sudden feeling of being cold | Great excitement about a new game | Being tired after school
exercise: The thief took the bike «without remorse». What does without remorse mean? | Sadly, with tears | *Cruelly, with no feeling of being sorry | Carefully, so nobody would notice | Quickly, with a big smile
exercise: Which feeling shows remorse? | Being bored in a long lesson | *Being sorry and wishing you had not done the wrong thing | Being proud of yourself for winning | Being hungry before lunch
test: «After he told a lie, Ravi felt remorse and went to apologise.» What did Ravi feel? | Surprise | Hunger | Happiness | *Remorse, a deep, sorry feeling for his wrong
test: What is remorse, in a short phrase? | A feeling of being happy | A kind of weather | *Deep sorrow for doing something wrong | A type of bird
exam: Toad felt remorse after his crimes, but it did not last long. What might this show? | Remorse is a kind of food | *Remorse can fade quickly if it is not followed by making things right | Remorse always lasts for ever | Toad could not feel anything at all
